course: dictionary
lesson: 8622
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «The actors learned their script for the school play.» Here the words around script (actors, play) show it means the written words that actors say.
explain: «Setup blocks belong at the top of a script; at the bottom they only run after everything else.» Blocks and run are clues. A script here is a list of instructions for a computer, not a play. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Script can also be a verb. To script something means to write it or plan it in detail. «Following the script» means doing what was planned, so something scripted was planned in advance. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then test it in the sentence.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A script can be the written words of a play, film or TV show.
fact: A script can also be a list of instructions for a computer, such as a short Scratch program.
fact: Script can mean a style of handwriting, such as joined-up writing, or a writing system like Latin or Cyrillic script.
fact: «Scripted» means planned in advance.
exercise: «The actors practised their lines from the script until they knew every word.» What is a script in this sentence? | *The written words of a play | A map with roads drawn on it | A loud noise in the hall | A kind of pet
exercise: «Her neat, joined-up script filled the whole page.» What does script mean here? | *A style of handwriting | A short holiday | A film about a school | A computer program
exercise: «The surprise party was scripted, so everyone knew exactly what to do.» What does scripted mean? | Hidden in a box | Written in pencil | *Planned in advance | Cancelled at the last minute
test: «Setup blocks belong at the top of a script.» In this sentence, what does script mean? | A style of handwriting | The words of a play | A rule about where to stand | *A list of instructions for a computer
test: To script something means to | Forget it on purpose | Draw a picture of it | Shout it loudly to a crowd | *Write it or plan it in detail
exam: Jayden says a script is only for plays. Is he right? | Yes, a script is only a kind of pet | Yes, a script is only ever the words of a play | No, a script can also be a computer program or a style of handwriting | *No, but only because a script is never written down
